---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="How opentier defines a 'real free tier' — inclusion and exclusion criteria."
  canonical="https://opentier.dev/methodology"
>
  <section class="container-narrow methodology-page">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Methodology</p>
      <h1>What counts as a free tier.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Not every service that says "free" deserves a slot in the catalog. Here's the bar.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Four tier types we list</h2>
      <dl class="tier-defs">
        <dt>Always free</dt>
        <dd>
          Permanent. No expiration, no time limit. Generally has a hard ceiling on usage (e.g., 10
          GB storage) but stays free forever within that ceiling.
        </dd>
        <dt>Free plan</dt>
        <dd>
          The free row of a multi-tier pricing page. Permanent. May require credit card after a
          grace period; we flag that explicitly.
        </dd>
        <dt>Trial credit</dt>
        <dd>
          A one-time credit balance (e.g., $25 to spend on the API) that funds free usage until
          depleted. Useful, but not the same as a permanent free tier.
        </dd>
        <dt>Pay as you go</dt>
        <dd>
          Per-use pricing with a meaningful free baseline (e.g., first N requests/month free).
          Common for usage-based services like LLM APIs.
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What we won't list</h2>
      <ul class="exclusion">
        <li>14-day trial that calls itself "free."</li>
        <li>"Free for non-commercial use only" that gates HTTPS or other essentials.</li>
        <li>Services requiring a credit card up front without disclosure.</li>
        <li>Tools abandoned for 18+ months (no commits, no marketing, no signs of life).</li>
        <li>
          "Lifetime deal" services on AppSumo that are not actually run by their maintainers
          anymore.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>When in doubt, we default to not listing.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Verification cadence</h2>
      <p>
        Every entry has a <code>date_verified</code> field. We re-verify entries at least once per month
        against the live pricing page. A weekly link-check workflow opens an issue if any URL goes 404.
        Entries unverified for more than 90 days get flagged.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Trust signals</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Every commit lives on <a
            href="https://github.com/Pratiyush/opentier"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a
          > — the entire history is public.
        </li>
        <li>Every change is gated by CI (schema validation, logo presence, build).</li>
        <li>No code is merged without a maintainer review.</li>
        <li>Every release is annotated and notes are published per tag.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </section>

  <style>
    .methodology-page {
      padding-top: var(--space-xl);
      padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    }
    .eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      color: var(--color-ink-soft);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    }
    .lede {
      margin-top: var(--space-md);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      color: var(--color-ink-soft);
      max-width: 56ch;
    }
    .block {
      padding: var(--space-lg) 0;
      border-top: var(--border-rule);
    }
    .block h2 {
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    }
    .tier-defs {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(140px, max-content) 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    }
    .tier-defs dt {
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--color-ink);
    }
    .tier-defs dd {
      color: var(--color-ink-soft);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .exclusion {
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-xs);
    }
    code {
      background: var(--color-paper-deep);
      padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
      border-radius: 3px;
      font-size: 0.92em;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
